Verdict: PASS. The fix does what the task asked: when grep can't search a path, yoyo grep now prints an error and exits 2 instead of saying "No matches found." and exiting 0. I wrote the verdict to session_plan/eval_task_2.md.

I ran the built binary from /tmp (uid 1001, so not root):

| Case | Output | Exit |
|---|---|---|
| yoyo grep zz9 /nonexistent_dir | Error: grep could not search ... (exit status 2) plus grep's "No such file or directory" | 2 |
| Search a chmod 000 directory | Same error, with grep's "Permission denied" | 2 |
| Real zero-match in a readable temp dir | No matches found. (same as before) | 0 |
| A search that matches | The match, unchanged | 0 |

On the four checklist items:
• **Does it match the task:** yes.
  • The error is decided from grep's exit status, not by reading its output: 0 or 1 is fine, anything else (including the process being killed) is an error.
  • grep's error text is cleaned with cli::sanitize_for_display and capped per line without cutting a character in half.
  • If some folders can't be read but others match, both the matches and the error are shown, and the exit is 2.
  • The `grep subcommand uses the same exit_if_nonzero approach as test/run`.
  • There is no in-process test of the arm that can exit the process; the old dispatch test now calls the status function directly.
• **Nothing added without being used:** every new type, function and constant is used in this diff. Both new modules are registered in `src/main.rs`, all existing callers were updated, and the module-size limit for commands_search.rs was raised to the new line count.
• **Docs:** `docs/src/usage/commands.md` has a new bullet explaining the error behaviour, and the `commands_search.rs` entry in `ARCHITECTURE.md` records the before/after results and the /find leftover.
• **Product behaviour:** the only user-visible change is this exit-code fix. The no-match exit stays 0 as the task required, and no config defaults or flags changed.

I didn't re-run the full test suite, since the harness already passed it. Clippy and the format check aren't in the build status I was given, so those two weren't confirmed here.

